      "description": "Watch Manchester United vs Manchester City highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 13, 2026. The Manchester derby returned to the spotlight on a tense afternoon at Old Trafford, as both sides looked to assert their dominance in a clash defined by tactical battles and high-stakes drama. With the atmosphere reaching fever pitch, the city rivals faced off in a game that would test their resilience to the limit. Early Shock and Defensive Discipline The match, held on September 13, 2026 , exploded into life with high intensity from the first whistle. However, the dynamics shifted dramatically in the 23rd minute when Manchester City were reduced to ten men. Phil Foden was shown a straight red card for violent conduct, forcing the visitors into a defensive reshuffle. Manchester United attempted to capitalize on the advantage, with Matheus Cunha and Bryan Mbeumo firing efforts from distance, but they failed to find the target. As the first half drew to a close, the tension boiled over on the touchline, resulting in a yellow card for Enzo Maresca for dissent. Haaland Delivers Amid VAR Drama Despite being a man down, the visitors remained a constant threat on the counter. In the 60th minute, Erling Haaland silenced the home crowd, finding the net with a powerful left-footed strike. The goal was subject to a lengthy VAR review, but the decision stood, sparking celebrations in the away end. Manchester United responded by introducing Benjamin Sesko and Joshua Zirkzee to bolster their attack. While they dominated possession with 55%, breaking through the City line led by Marc Guehi proved to be an arduous task. Late Scares and Donnarumma's Heroics The closing stages were marred by a flurry of bookings as Harry Maguire , Enzo Fernandez , and Josko Gvardiol were all cautioned. In the fifth minute of stoppage time, United had a golden opportunity to level the score. Bruno Fernandes teed up Bryan Mbeumo for what looked like a certain goal, but Gianluigi Donnarumma produced a world-class save to deny the hosts. Despite late pressure and numerous corners, the ten men of City held firm in front of 74,161 spectators to claim a hard-fought derby victory."
